From 1f72028cef6c56ca513c0cc5e4b40f1efc3478f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rama Krishna Phani A <ramkri@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 20:45:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] PCIe: qcom-ecam: Fix Global IRQ management for dynamic
 init/deinit

Move Global IRQ request from probe to init and add proper release in
deinit to support controller reset/re-initialization via sysfs.

Previously, IRQ was requested once during probe and never released,
causing -EBUSY on subsequent init attempts. Now IRQ is requested after
successful PCI host probe and released during deinit, enabling multiple
init/deinit cycles.

Also extract qcom_pcie_clear_safety_interrupts() helper and improve
IRQ thread pre-init protection to prevent races with concurrent deinit.

Change-Id: If7648966aa7071ef75a810e44f7eb4add0a9a30e
Signed-off-by: Rama Krishna Phani A <ramkri@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-qcom-ecam.c | 366 ++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 208 insertions(+), 158 deletions(-)

